{"main_category": "Digital Music", "title": "Rio Angie", "average_rating": 5.0, "rating_number": 1, "features": [], "description": ["Shrimp City Slim (aka Gary Erwin, b. 1953, Chicago) has long been associated with the Southeastern blues scene. However, he's always written songs in a variety of styles and 'Rio Angie' touches on that side of the artist. This solo piano CD contains improvisations on eleven original themes from 1971-1980, inspired in part by travels in Mexico and South America. He's recently been working these pieces into his solo blues piano shows and audiences have taken notice. Here then is what you've been asking for...a cool, dreamy album that will hopefully relax and engage you."], "price": 14.98, "images": [{"thumb": "https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61YOfb2kjsL._SS40_.jpg", "large": "https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61YOfb2kjsL.jpg", "variant": "MAIN", "hi_res": "https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/71O2Wd9XWlL._SL1000_.jpg"}], "videos": [], "store": "Shrimp City Slim  (Artist)    Format: Audio CD", "categories": ["CDs & Vinyl", "Jazz", "Avant Garde & Free Jazz"], "details": {"Product Dimensions": "5.6 x 0.4 x 4.9 inches; 4 Ounces", "Manufacturer": "CD Baby", "Original Release Date": "2012", "Date First Available": "August 20, 2012", "Label": "CD Baby", "Country of Origin": "USA", "Number of discs": "1"}, "parent_asin": "B00902T10Y", "bought_together": null}
